# What the drive commands refuse, in DOS's words.
program: shell
keys: dir nothing\ntype\ntype c:\\docs\ndir c:\\readme.txt\\x\ntype a:bad*name\ntype a:toolongname.txt\nz:\ndir q:\n
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs mame
---
rx286, test build
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
A:\>dir nothing
File not found
A:\>type
Required parameter missing
A:\>type c:\docs
Access denied
A:\>dir c:\readme.txt\x
Path not found
A:\>type a:bad*name
Invalid path
A:\>type a:toolongname.txt
Invalid path
A:\>z:
Invalid drive specification
A:\>dir q:
Invalid drive specification
A:\>
